{"id": "section-body-10185", "title": "Cholecystitis", "chapterId": "chapter-ten", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "GASTROINTESTINAL DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Disorders of The Liver and Biliary Tract", "Cholecystitis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-10185", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Cholecystitis", "runs": [{"text": "Cholecystitis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1460"}}, {"id": "body-10186", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cholecystitis is inflammation of the gallbladder that occurs most commonly because of an obstruction of the cystic duct by gallstones (stone impaction in cystic duct leads to inflammation behind obstruction causing GB swelling and secondary infection of biliary fluid).", "runs": [{"text": "Cholecystitis is inflammation of the gallbladder that occurs most commonly because of an obstruction of the cystic duct by gallstones"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(stone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "impaction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cystic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "duct"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leads"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inflammation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "behind"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "obstruction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "GB"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swelling"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection of biliary fluid)."}]}, {"id": "body-10188", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Acalculous cholecystitis: Occurs in critically ill. GB stasis and ischemia (without cholelithiasis) leading to necroinflammation.", "runs": [{"text": "Acalculous", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "cholecystitis:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Occurs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "critically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text"